{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c515","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a08900-d199-7822-974c-1de7f95bc0fc"},"sequence":229,"recorded_at":1780531400000453,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"0a8bdc02-b2cf-4bed-86b9-db3127962aef","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"0a8bdc02-b2cf-4bed-86b9-db3127962aef","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"0a8bdc02-b2cf-4bed-86b9-db3127962aef"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a08901-6b32-7101-a94f-f78883a377d8"},"task_id":"01a08901-6b32-7101-a94f-f78883a377d8","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a08901-6b32-7101-a94f-f78883a377d8","chunk":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-7-1\",\n  \"command\": \"cat /Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.task-board/.resources/TASK-260909-2ez769/TASK-260909-2ez769_results.md 2>&1 | head -c 8000\\necho \\\"\\\"\\necho \\\"===RETRY2===\\\"\\ncat /Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.task-board/.resources/TASK-260909-2ez769/TASK-260909-2ez769_retry2.md 2>&1 | head -c 5000\\necho \\\"\\\"\\necho \\\"===REVIEWER===\\\"\\ncat /Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.task-board/.resources/TASK-260909-2ez769/TASK-260909-2ez769_reviewer.md 2>&1 | head -c 4000\\necho \\\"\\\"\\necho \\\"===PRESERVATION OUTCOME===\\\"\\ncat /Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.task-board/.resources/TASK-260830-z1yxg9/TASK-260830-z1yxg9_preservation-before-credentials-260910.md 2>&1 | head -c 4000\",\n  \"description\": \"Read prior results and reviewer feedback\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"# TASK-260909-2ez769 results — Host Trust Store 1.0.0 + Config 4.0.0 migration\\n\\nProducer: developer run RUN-260910-cc2077, 2026-09-10. Worktree left UNCOMMITTED\\non task-board/story/STORY-260830-1kiyj6 for handoff snapshot (no producer commit).\\n\\n## Resume precondition (verified, not assumed)\\n\\n- STORY-260908-18woqo landed on origin/main: 5d98b08 + d727513, both\\n  `git verify-commit` Good (oparin@me.com). v0.6.0 lock on main pins\\n  spec commit 0cbdf100dbf84df50c64f792b1f940e3a67859a6, Configuration\\n  1.0.0-4.0.0. Normative text consumed read-only from\\n  origin/main:internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.6.0.md (sections 6.6, 11.10.2-11.10.5).\\n\\n## Foreign RPC delta (preserved, verified, parked)\\n\\n- All 15 enumerated bytes verified ALL-MATCH against\\n  .temp/TASK-260830-z1yxg9/preserved-before-credentials-260910/manifest.json\\n  before any change; tracked.patch proven byte-identical to `git diff`;\\n  files/ copies verified BACKUP-ALL-MATCH; all modes 100644.\\n- Preservation outcome attached to TASK-260830-z1yxg9\\n  (TASK-260830-z1yxg9_preservation-before-credentials-260910.md) BEFORE\\n  separation, with restoration instructions.\\n- Parked ONLY the enumerated delta: 4 tracked paths restored to checkpoint\\n  blobs (worktree-blob == checkpoint-blob verified per path), 11 untracked\\n  files moved to .temp/TASK-260909-2ez769/parked-rpc-delta-260910/ (bytes\\n  re-verified against manifest). Worktree was CLEAN after parking.\\n- RPC task left pending/blocked; nothing from the delta was consumed.\\n\\n## Base transition (attempted, refused, recorded)\\n\\n- `task-board worktree refresh-candidate TASK-260909-2ez769` refused:\\n  \\\"candidate refresh requires the final unresolved leaf\\\". Exact refusal kept.\\n- No manual rebase/merge/switch performed (Story workspace forbids it).\\n- Implementation therefore sits on checkpoint base c1eff01 (v0.5.0 pin +\\n  checkpointed SSH/peer-identity leaves) while citing v0.6.0 normatively.\\n  Adoption files (specpin v0.6.0, SPEC.v0.6.0.md, catalogue, cigate) were\\n  deliberately NOT duplicated; integration must land this onto the adoption\\n  base. New code references v0.6.0 by value, not by the adopted pin.\\n\\n## What was built\\n\\n- internal/hosttrust (new): TrustStore 1.0.0 closed reader/writer\\n  (exact keys, duplicate-JSON-key audit, uint53 generation, sorted entries,\\n  canonical DER, retire_at exactly-for-retiring); Profile-1 issuance\\n  (fresh P-256 keys, exact CN/SAN/KU/EKU/BC/SKI/AKI/serials/validity,\\n  root key destroyed) and verification (inclusive validity, no skew/grace);\\n  owner-only custody (0700/0600, owner, no symlinks, verify-never-repair,\\n  flock SH/EX lock); atomic crash-durable commits (stage+fsync+rename+dirsync,\\n  staging ignored, corrupt never empty); explicit enrollment with OOB tuple\\n  reproduction; fresh-key bounded rotation (24h cap, leaf-expiry cap, no\\n  second rotation, MarkRetiring for peer catch-up); revocation tombstones\\n  with generation bump; current-generation dispatch/mutation authorization\\n  (binding check, exact leaf/root/SPKI match, allowlist, hello equality,\\n  EX-serialized boundaries); public-only enrollment export; replication\\n  exclusion registry; redacted renderings throughout.\\n- internal/config: Version4/TransportSSHTLS13/HostChannelVersion constants;\\n  closed rawV4 reader (required transport, no default; required closed\\n  host_channel; no per-peer override; no cert bytes possible by shape);\\n  v4 validation; EncodeVersion4 (defence-in-depth re-read); EncodeCurrent\\n  refuses v4 values; Migrate→v4 refuses toward Preview/Apply;\\n  Migrate v4→v3 refuses as downgrade; AssessCompatibility v4/v4 compatible,\\n  v3-reader read-only; PreviewV4 (v3-only source, admitted credential,\\n  complete peer enrollment or named drops, exact bytes); ApplyV4 (confirm,\\n  source/gen/bytes/custody re-validation, backup, generation-bump commit\\n  with config recovery); RollbackV4 (ack, backup-only, generation bump,\\n  idempotent no-op).\\n- interop: v4 snapshots flow through peeridentity.FromSnapshot unchanged\\n  (internal/peeridentity/v4_interop_test.go).\\n- census: secprim roster extended to hosttrust package + 5 disposition rows\\n  (40 sites); redaction/error-identity discipline preserved.\\n\\n## AC coverage: 21 of 21 rows driven through production entry points\\n\\nReader: config.Decode (schema_v4 tests), hosttrust.DecodeTrust (trust tests).\\nRefusals missing/partial/unreadable/ambiguous/downgraded: store + preview +\\napply + rollback absent/corrupt/dup/legacy cases. No legacy fallback:\\nrequired transport, Migrate-v4-explicit, EncodeCurrent-v4 refusal, v3-reader\\nread-only. Enrollment/mapping/rotation/revocation/generation-auth: lifecycle\\n+ authorize tests. Owner-only atomic crash-durable writes: custody tests incl.\\nfault-seam commit failure, staging discipline, trust-commit recovery.\\nExact-preview migration + peer enrollment + durable apply/rollback: preview,\\napply, rollback tests. Preservation: full existing suites green unmodified +\\ninterop test. Platform/crash evidence: darwin 0700/0600/owner/symlink/fault\\ntests (this run). No secret replication: exclusion registry + walk test +\\ncensus rows + redaction tests.\\nStated bounds (not production-driven here): live TLS 1.3 launch/handshake/\\nhello/dispatch and stream close-down belong to the RPC transport task\\n(sections 11.10.1/11.10.4 transport gates); Windows DACL beyond owner-SID\\nequality has no runner here (code builds for windows, unix fully enforced);\\npeer-side distribution of enrollment/rotation/revocation is operator duty per\\nspec; server-flag refusals (no-host-channel) have no call site in this base.\\n\\n## Negative + mutation evidence (truthful counts)\\n\\n- hosttrust/mutations.py: 11 narrowing mutants killed by named tests, 1\\n  neutral SURVIVED control. config/mutations_v4.py: 3 narrowing + 1\\n  label-precision mutant killed, 1 neutral SURVIVED control.\\n- No gate searches source text for a token (all gates operate on decoded\\n  values/DER/parsed TOML), so the preserve-token behavioral-mutant clause is\\n  vacuous; stated here, not silently skipped.\\n- Evidence preserved: .temp/TASK-260909-2ez769/mutations-hosttrust/ and\\n  mutations-config/ (results.json, table.md, manifest.json with source\\n  digests and per-mutant exit/test lists).\\n- Gates: go build ./... ok; go vet ./... clean; gofmt clean;\\n  go test ./... -count=1 all ok; go test ./... -cover all ok\\n  (hosttrust 76.5%, config 93.2%; remainder is fault-branch/error-path\\n  plumbing and Windows-only files); 245 top-level tests pass across the four\\n  touched packages; config refusal-inventory audit passes (3 justified\\n  defence-in-depth subsumptions pinned in-file); secprim census passes.\\n\\n## Notes for reviewer/integrator\\n\\n- MarkRetiring was added during testing: peer rotation catch-up had no local\\n  path (only self-rotation existed). It bounds a peer entry with the same\\n  24h/enrolled_at rules.\\n- ensureOwnerDir verifies existing directories and never repairs them:\\n  silently narrowing a widened directory would mask the violation (found by\\n  TestCustodyRefusals).\\n- Secret-census blind spot (honest): LeafKeyDER and \\\"private-key.pem\\\" evade\\n  the token list (\\\"key\\\" alone is not a token; hyphen vs underscore). Not\\n  widening the token list here (would re-derive the whole repo); covered by\\n  TestNoSecretReplication + redaction tests instead.\\n- Untracked candidates for review: internal/hosttrust/*,\\n  internal/config/migration_v4*.go + schema_v4_test.go +\\n  migration_v4_test.go + migration_v4_apply_test.go + mutations_v4.py,\\n  internal/peeridentity/v4_interop_test.go. Tracked edits: config migration/\\n  schema/validation/writer, refusal pin, secprim census rows.\\n\\n===RETRY2===\\n# TASK-260909-2ez769 retry outcome (RUN-260910-cdbb05, attempt 1/3)\\n\\nProducer retry after CR rev1 `changes_requested`: rev1 validation failed at\\ncommand 21/26. Candidate code is unchanged since rev1 (tracked diff and\\nuntracked list byte-identical to pre-run backup). Worktree left UNCOMMITTED\\nfor snapshot; no producer commit (branch still at checkpoint c1eff01).\\n\\n## rev1 failure: root cause (evidence-backed, external to candidate)\\n\\nFailing command (byte-exact from `TASK-260909-2ez769_change-request_rev1-validation.log`):\\n\\n```\\n$ go run ./internal/catalog/cmd/cataloggen -metadata internal/catalog/catalog.v0.6.0.json -contracts internal/specpin/v0.6.0.lock.json -output internal/catalog/catalog_gen.go -check\\nread metadata: open internal/catalog/catalog.v0.6.0.json: no such file or directory\\nexit status 1\\n[exit 1]\\nsuite stopped at command 21 of 26\\n```\\n\\n- Commands 1-20 (gofmt, build, vet, `go test ./... -v/-race/-cover`,\\n  13 fuzz gates, tracecheck) all exited 0 on the rev1 tree.\\n- The command fails reading its INPUT files, before any comparison. No\\n  candidate-side change can satisfy an input-file existence check except\\n  adding the adoption files, which is forbidden absorption (see below).\\n- `internal/catalog/catalog.v0.6.0.json` and\\n  `internal/specpin/v0.6.0.lock.json` exist on `origin/main`\\n  (adoption STORY-260908-18woqo, 5d98b08, landed 2026-09-09) but not on\\n  this story base (checkpoint c1eff01, 2026-09-08, v0.5.0 pin).\\n- The suite tracks current main: pre-adoption validation\\n  (TASK-260908-2tkufa rev1, Sept 9) ran the same slot with\\n  `catalog.v0.5.0.json`; post-adoption runs use v0.6.0. Sibling proof that\\n  the slot passes on an adoption base: TASK-260830-21gygk rev1 passed\\n  command 21 (v0.6.0 check) and stopped later at command 24 on an\\n  unrelated review-probes JSON issue.\\n\\n## Managed base transition: refused again (exact refusal recorded)\\n\\n```\\n$ task-board worktree refresh-candidate TASK-260909-2ez769\\ncandidate refresh requires the final unresolved leaf\\n```\\n\\nSame refusal as the prior run (RUN-260910-cc2077). Manual rebase/merge is\\nforbidden in the Story workspace, and vendoring adoption files into this\\ncandidate is forbidden absorption (prior outcome: adoption files\\ndeliberately not duplicated; integration must land onto the adoption\\nbase). Per the producer brief this refusal is reported to root so the\\nreusable tool