{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000d7ff","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a08900-d199-7822-974c-1de7f95bc0fc"},"sequence":2650,"recorded_at":1780531400005295,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"0a8bdc02-b2cf-4bed-86b9-db3127962aef","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"0a8bdc02-b2cf-4bed-86b9-db3127962aef","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"0a8bdc02-b2cf-4bed-86b9-db3127962aef"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a08912-67a3-7331-bea7-c222c57c6a1f"},"task_id":"01a08912-67a3-7331-bea7-c222c57c6a1f","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a08912-67a3-7331-bea7-c222c57c6a1f","chunk":"edited\nchanged lines: lines 1-6\n--- original\n+++ updated\n@@\n-# Flight Logbook\n-\n-> Institutional memory. Concise, factual, high-signal.\n-> Newest entries first. One block per insight.\n-\n-## 2026-09-10\n+# Flight Logbook\n+\n+> Institutional memory. Concise, factual, high-signal.\n+> Newest entries first. One block per insight.\n+\n+## 2026-09-10 (later)\n+\n+### TASK-260909-2ez769 retry — closed-reader hardening + mutation refresh\n+- SCOPE: same candidate; new gates only in `internal/hosttrust` + 1 census row. No config-package behavior change.\n+- FINDING: `DecodeTrust` never bound identifiers to bytes (crafted/corrupt store with swapped digests decoded) and never checked cross-entry leaf/key/root uniqueness at read time; fixed in `trust_decode.go`/`trust.go` with 5 new refusal rows.\n+- FINDING: `MarkRetiring` (peer catch-up path) missed the no-later-than-old-leaf-expiry cap that `Rotate` enforces; added with `TestMarkRetiringCapsAtLeafExpiry`.\n+- FINDING: `ValidateCustody` never bound the contained leaf to the credential directory name (valid credential filed under another name passed); added digest-vs-dir check with `TestValidateCustodyBindsDirectory`.\n+- FINDING: old `unsorted entries` refusal fixture was malformed JSON (refused on shape, never reached the ordering check); replaced with a genuinely descending valid pair. The `>=`-to-`>` sort mutant stopped killing once the mapping gate subsumed identical entries; re-aimed to `==` (admits unsorted-but-distinct) killing via the genuine fixture.\n+- FINDING: `AuthorizeDispatch` doc overclaimed same-lock check+dispatch; corrected to the actual guarantee (coherent check under shared lock; caller binds generation + watchdog; mutations use exclusive `WithMutationAuthorization`). Stale `transact` missing-store comment and `TOML/JSON` error comment fixed.\n+- VALIDATION (this run): `go build ./...` 0; `go vet` touched pkgs 0; `gofmt` clean; `go test ./... -count=1` all ok; `go test ./... -cover` all ok (hosttrust 77.0%, config 93.2%, peeridentity 97.5%, secprim 94.4%); hosttrust harness 15 narrowing killed + neutral passed; config harness 4 killed + neutral passed; census + refusal-inventory green.\n+- BLOCKER (unchanged, external): CR validation command 21/26 needs adoption files absent on story base c1eff01; `refresh-candidate` still refuses (\"requires the final unresolved leaf\"). No vendoring, no manual rebase. Candidate left UNCOMMITTED for snapshot.\n+\n+## 2026-09-10\n","final_result":true}}}
